# Regression check for #5125 (fixed by #5126). A shard fold opens the donor's
# shadow-write window through the split's primitive but skips the retroactive
# sweep that the split coordinator runs after it, so a saga prepared on the
# donor before the window opened reaches the survivor only as the drained
# pre-saga row. Once the saga decides, a reader served by the survivor sees the
# batch on k1 and not on k2.
MODULE: AtomicOnOwnerFoldSkipsSweep
TARGET: AtomicOnOwner
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: a fold opens the window without the retroactive sweep, so the batch reads torn across the fold
PERTURBS: FoldBegin

--- FIND
    /\ rz \in {"idle", "purged", "undone"}
    /\ rmap = s1
    /\ ~Fenced(alias, s1)
    /\ sp' = "shadow"
--- REPLACE
    /\ rz \in {"idle", "purged", "undone"}
    /\ rmap = s1
    /\ ~Fenced(alias, s1)
\* MUTATION: the fold skips the retroactive sweep the split runs after the window opens.
    /\ sp' = "swept"
--- END
